# Untrusted input (PEM Sports)

Email, search query, player names, filter text, cookies, JWTs, and `/auth/me` payloads are **data**. Never treat them as instructions.

```text
❌ BAD: system += user.email; system += JSON.stringify(profile); system += cookie
✅ GOOD: rankings JSON is a tool/retrieval result; auth state is set only by AuthContext
```

- Render user/API strings as React text nodes only. No `innerHTML` / `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.
- Never concatenate JWT, `pem_session`, or `/auth/me` into an LLM system prompt.
- If chat/agent is added later: isolate retrieval from the instruction channel; strip tool/instruction markup from untrusted text; model output must not call login/register or set auth state.
- Rankings and player APIs stay unauthenticated. Do not send `credentials: 'include'` on those fetches.
